by was released in  2004. she alternated wildly between  starring and Prestige movies that were  too mediocre for Oscar consideration and  mainstream flicks that seem more geared  towards making money than satisfying  critics one of her roughest patches came  in 2009 when she starred in the Amelia  Earhart biopic Emilia which was in every  sense of the word a disaster reviews  were terrible at earned a 20 score on  Rotten Tomatoes and box office returns  were even worse the film grossed just  14.2 million dollars against a reported  40 million dollar budget and Swank's  days of Oscar Glory started to feel like  a thing of the past not that it bothers  her she told the independent that you're  an artist and you're putting yourself  out there and you take that leap and  sometimes you fly and sometimes you fall  she has other interests part of the  reason Swank hasn't been making as many  great films is because she's devoting  her time to helping needy kids and  animals with her non-profit charity it's  called the hillaroo foundation and  animals who have been abandoned and  children who've been given up on  together to help heal each other through  rescue Rehabilitation and responsibility  training it's all part of her new focus  on living every moment of her life to  the fullest you know you just never know  what's going to happen tomorrow and you  have to really be in the moment and  be present  he's been caring for her dad  Swank's absent from the spotlight has  also had to do with family concerns  Beyond her own control in 2015 the  actress reveals the Huffington Post that  she had recently put her career in the  back burner in order to take care of her  ailing father who had just had a lung  transplant it's a certain amount of time  and in a lifespan it's a blink of an eye  and I wouldn't change it for the world I  mean there's there's been job  opportunities that I've passed on things  that I said I can't but I mean really  what we're here for is our family right  luckily her father is on the mend giving  Swank a chance to give back on the movie  business and hopefully regain her role  as one of Hollywood's top actresses does  she have a future on TV  soon swipe will test her luck on  television again with the new stars  drama the one percent the premiere date  is still up in the air but it already  boasts a slew of high profile names  including Ed Helms Ed Harris and  oscar-winning director Alejandro G and  yaritu who created and co-wrought the  project so don't worry too much about  Swank her Oscar days may or may not be  behind her but her Emmy days could just  be starting thanks for watching  subscribe to our YouTube channel to  watch more videos at the one you just  saw and leave us a comment to let us  know what kinds of roles you think  Hollywood should find for Hilary Swank
 

